+    """Shell snippet that installs Node >= 20 and leaves it on PATH.
+
+    The musl path is where this kept going wrong: nodejs.org publishes no musl
+    build; the UNOFFICIAL musl build of node 22 needs a newer libstdc++ than the
+    sweap-images Alpine 3.18 bases carry, so it installs and then dies with
+    `Error relocating ... symbol not found`; and those bases ship no curl at all.
+    So try apk's own `nodejs-current` (20.8.1 on 3.18, linked against the
+    libstdc++ that is actually installed) first, and fall back to the tarball via
+    curl or busybox wget only if that is still < 20. glibc keeps using nvm.
+
+    The >= 20 gate is hard either way: these CLIs import `aborted` from node:util
+    (node >= 19.7) and fail at RUNTIME, not install, on anything older.
+    """
+    script = r"""if command -v apk >/dev/null 2>&1 || ldd --version 2>&1 | grep -qi musl; then
